        detailed: 'Technical deliverability rests on DNS authentication plus positive recipient engagement signals. SPF specifies authorized sending servers; DKIM attaches a cryptographic signature proving emails weren’t tampered in transit; DMARC aligns both with domain handling policy. Clean list hygiene regularly suppresses hard bounces, honors immediate 1-click unsubscribes, and runs Sunset Policies pruning chronically unengaged contacts.',
        concepts: '- SPF (Sender Policy Framework): DNS allowlist of authorized mail IPs/providers.\n- DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail): Cryptographic email header signature verifying authenticity.\n- DMARC: Policy unifying SPF/DKIM alignment against spoofing.\n- Hard Bounce: Permanent undeliverable invalid address needing immediate removal.',
        steps: 'Step 1: Configure custom sending domain DNS records (SPF, DKIM, DMARC).\nStep 2: Maintain clean visible 1-click Unsubscribe footer (builds trust, lowers Spam button clicks!).\nStep 3: Monitor Spam Complaint Rate strictly below 0.1%.\nStep 4: Run quarterly Sunset Re-engagement & Suppress silent contacts.',
