        title: 'BLUF Executive Writing & Effective Meeting Hygiene',
        intro: 'Clear written communication saves teams hours weekly by preventing back-and-forth confusion, missed deadlines, and bloated meetings.',
        simple: 'Imagine reading a mystery novel just to find out whether you need an umbrella today! Put the weather forecast in line 1 ("Take an umbrella today — heavy rain at 3 PM"), then list radar details underneath.',
        detailed: 'BLUF (Bottom Line Up Front) puts your core decision, status (`On Track` / `At Risk`), or explicit request (`Please approve by Friday`) in the very first sentence, using bold headers and numbered options underneath. Apply equal discipline to meetings: every invite requires an objective and clear decision list beforehand, followed by written Owner + Due Date takeaways afterward.',
        concepts: '- BLUF (Bottom Line Up Front): Leading with conclusions/asks before supporting narrative.\n- Async First: Using crisp shared docs/memos when no live brainstorm/debate is needed.\n- Action Register: Simple What / Who / By-When follow-up recap after every sync.',
        steps: 'Step 1: Decide exact reader outcome before typing (Approve, Read FYI, Answer Question).\nStep 2: State outcome + deadline in Opening Sentence + Subject Line.\nStep 3: Bullet 2–4 concise supporting facts/options below.\nStep 4: Keep meetings strictly agenda-bound and recap owners within 2 hours.',
