        longQ: 'Q: Transform a vague 45-minute weekly "Sync Call" invite into a tight, effective 20-minute async-supported decision meeting protocol.\nAnswer Outline: Share written status doc 24h prior (async pre-read); reserve live 20 mins strictly for 2 unresolved trade-off decisions; assign clear timekeeper; post concise 3-bullet Owner/Date summary right after.',
        mcq: '1. Effective BLUF email structure opens immediately with:\nA) Main recommendation, status, or explicit ask & deadline  B) Personal weather chit-chat for 3 paragraphs  C) Unlabeled raw screenshots  D) Footnotes\nAnswer: A (Respects reader time and clarifies action immediately.)\n2. Which post-meeting habit prevents forgotten promises?\nA) Sending a crisp written recap listing Task, Single Owner, and Deadline  B) Waiting silently until next month  C) Inviting 12 extra spectators  D) Skipping notes\nAnswer: A (Clear single accountability drives follow-through.)',
        campaignExample: 'Operational Productivity Lift: Team replaced unstructured 6-person status calls with weekly BLUF Friday memos + 15-min exception huddles—freeing 4 hours/week per specialist.',
        toolsStrategies: 'BLUF Email Template, Pre-Read Agenda Structure, What/Who/When Action Matrix.',
        planningExercise: 'Rewrite one past long message or assignment request into crisp BLUF format (<75 words) including bold Ask + Deadline.',
